ce-510c28e0bc46","position":{"commit_sha":"0c260c294c49039d9671bdcd7a1a6bcb4c5c1c5b","position":"1785962250981352001-f57baf9c-379a-4274-afce-510c28e0bc46"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2dde5866c9b57fdf65e002c8204c5ff803699e99db0ef36379990d01f34520c6","event_uuid":"59dc1add-78ef-4838-adc5-45406b6a081e","position":{"commit_sha":"0c260c294c49039d9671bdcd7a1a6bcb4c5c1c5b","position":"1785962251541208001-59dc1add-78ef-4838-adc5-45406b6a081e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9c4fcd41e27697e05bc7f1cf1549c154823ae7bfdf60971b9806acde3972ea5d","event_uuid":"672960bb-02a2-4885-bda5-74a0ccf7c633","position":{"commit_sha":"b6ab84deb764d45170e65c2dfb67d0ebd8253942","position":"1785962270559052001-672960bb-02a2-4885-bda5-74a0ccf7c633"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-222_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"4cf58ecd-8513-4de1-a7b6-62b672e02919","comments":[],"created_at":1785957922659459001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0b97ee89-359a-4f8f-9227-cdba9d023bb1","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"03ef-6fb5-158b-4abd"},{"link_uuid":"672960bb-02a2-4885-bda5-74a0ccf7c633","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0c55-4493-b95a-47a4"}],"description":"Discovered while implementing 03ef-6fb5-158b-4abd (scheduled mirror main CI).\n\n## Context\n\nBefore 03ef, `codeql.yml` ran on every push to `main` PLUS a weekly schedule, and its own\ncomment described the weekly cron as catching \"advisories that land between pushes\" — i.e. the\npush trigger was the primary scan of new code and the schedule was the backstop for newly\npublished advisories.\n\n03ef dropped the push trigger from every workflow so the mirror's `main` CI reports branch\nhealth on a schedule rather than per-commit. CodeQL was NOT moved onto the new 6-hourly tick at\nthat time; the workflow header asserted that a 6-hourly cadence would be \"a 28x increase nobody\nasked for\". That left the weekly cron as CodeQL's PRIMARY scan of newly-landed code rather than\na between-pushes backstop, so a newly-introduced SAST finding could sit unscanned for up to 7\ndays.\n\n## The decision (made by the operator — settled, not open)\n\n**CodeQL moves to the 6-hourly tick.** The operator's instruction, verbatim: \"CodeQL should be\nrunning every 6 hours, which is the cadence I specified for scheduled CI to replace push on\nmain.\"\n\nReasoning recorded:\n\n* The 6-hourly tick was specified as the **replacement for push-on-main**. CodeQL's original\n  design ran it on every push to `main`; leaving it weekly silently *reduced* its coverage of\n  newly-landed code rather than preserving it. Joining the tick restores the intended posture.\n* The \"28x cost increase\" rationale in the current header **does not apply**: `navapbc/rebar`\n  is a **public** repository, and both CodeQL and GitHub Actions minutes are **free** for public\n  repos. The frequency argument was therefore not a billing constraint.\n* Worst-case exposure for a newly-introduced SAST finding drops from 7 days to 6 hours.\n\n## Implementation plan\n\n1. `.github/workflows/codeql.yml`\n   * Replace the weekly cron `23 4 * * 1` with a 6-hourly cron **`35 */6 * * *`**. The minute is\n     off-the-hour (never `0`/`30`) and **distinct from every sibling lane** — `test.yml` is `41`,\n     `optionality.yml` is `47`, `verify-identity.yml` is `53` — so the four branch-health lanes\n     stay staggered on a 6-minute spacing (35/41/47/53) and none of them pile onto the hour\n     boundary that GitHub's scheduler congests.\n   * Rewrite the header comment. It currently asserts CodeQL deliberately does NOT join the\n     6-hourly tick and cites a 28x cost increase; both statements become **false** with this\n     change. A stale comment contradicting the config it sits above is itself a defect.\n   * Everything else is unchanged: no `push` trigger is reintroduced, `workflow_dispatch` stays,\n     permissions/concurrency/matrix/steps untouched.\n\n2. `tests/unit/test_ci_main_push_policy.py` — existing coverage pins the OLD cadence and will\n   go red. **Retarget it; do not delete it.**\n   * Move `codeql.yml` out of the `_OWN_CADENCE` map (which asserts a lane keeps a slower cron\n     AND carries no `*/6` cron) and into the 6-hourly cohort.\n   * Because CodeQL — unlike the other three lanes — has **no push trigger at all**, it cannot\n     join the `_SIX_HOURLY` tuple wholesale: that tuple also drives the \"push CI for non-main\n     branches is preserved\" case, which CodeQL would fail. Introduce a separate\n     schedule-only cohort so the cadence assertion covers CodeQL while the push-preservation\n     assertion does not.\n   * Keep every assertion that still holds: CodeQL runs on **no** push to `main`, and CodeQL\n     keeps `workflow_dispatch` (both driven by `_NO_MAIN_PUSH`, which must still include it).\n   * Add cover for the staggering invariant the operator specified: the 6-hourly lanes use\n     **distinct** off-the-hour minutes.\n   * Update the module docstring, which currently states the CodeQL scan \"stays weekly\".\n\n## Out of scope (explicitly not touched)\n\n`gerrit-verify.yaml`, both reconcilers, `external-integration.yml`, `mirror-guard.yml`, every\n`_*.yml` reusable, `prompt-eval.yml` (billable live-LLM tier — stays weekly), and\n`terraform-drift.yml` (stays daily).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The cadence question is decided explicitly, with the reasoning recorded (above).\n- [ ] `.github/workflows/codeql.yml` schedules `35 */6 * * *` and no longer carries `23 4 * * 1`.\n- [ ] `codeql.yml`'s header comment states the new rationale and no longer asserts that CodeQL\n      stays off the 6-hourly tick or that the cadence is a cost tradeoff.\n- [ ] `codeql.yml` still has no `push` trigger and still has `workflow_dispatch`.\n- [ ] The four 6-hourly lanes (`test.yml`, `optionality.yml`, `verify-identity.yml`,\n      `codeql.yml`) use distinct, off-the-hour minutes.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_ci_main_push_policy.py` pins the new cadence instead of the old one, with\n      its no-push and `workflow_dispatch` cover retained, and passes.\n- [ ] `prompt-eval.yml` (weekly) and `terraform-drift.yml` (daily) are unchanged, still pinned.\n- [ ] `make check` is green.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","0c55-4493-b95a-47a4"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"f57baf9c-379a-4274-afce-510c28e0bc46","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"34b5-ad7d-b983-47f9","ticket_type":"task","title":"Decide whether CodeQL's weekly cadence is still right now that it no longer runs on push to main","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b14b34be-e7c8-4307-8e4a-b7b472bf6a2b","0b97ee89-359a-4f8f-9227-cdba9d023bb1","b0bbd2bb-e1a6-4ed8-8c47-6b7e05770c36","c43ce582-1d54-4074-aea6-a14ada534d12","f57baf9c-379a-4274-afce-510c28e0bc46","59dc1add-78ef-4838-adc5-45406b6a081e","672960bb-02a2-4885-bda5-74a0ccf7c633"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785962270559052002,"uuid":"58cd6226-8d15-4fd6-8652-e25f969609f7"}